4)You've noticed that several ImagePullBackOff errors are occurring in pods across different namespaces. What could be the common causes and how would you investigate?
When ImagePullBackOff happens across multiple namespaces, I would look for cluster-wide issues like registry authentication failures, registry unavailability, 
network or proxy changes, or node-level pull issues.
I start by checking pod events, validating image tags, confirming imagePullSecrets, verifying internal registry health, and ensuring nodes can reach registries.
Often the root cause is expired pull credentials or internal registry/storage issues.”
